Subject: [PATCH] network: unregister BSS objects before removing their network

ELL unregisters only the named object, not its descendants. Removing a station
frees its scan BSS structures after removing the networks, leaving the child
BasicServiceSet objects registered with dangling pointers. A subsequent
ObjectManager.GetManagedObjects call can crash in network_bss_property_get_address.

Unregister each network's BSS children before removing the network object.
This preserves valid property backing data until the objects are unregistered.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/network.c
+++ b/src/network.c
@@ -1909,6 +1909,7 @@
 static void network_unregister(struct network *network, int reason)
 {
 	struct l_dbus *dbus = dbus_get_bus();
+	const struct l_queue_entry *entry;
 
 	if (network->connect_after_anqp)
 		dbus_pending_reply(&network->connect_after_anqp,
@@ -1920,6 +1921,12 @@
 
 	agent_request_cancel(network->agent_request, reason);
 	network_settings_close(network);
+
+	/* Removing a parent object does not unregister its BSS children. */
+	for (entry = l_queue_get_entries(network->bss_list); entry;
+			entry = entry->next)
+		l_dbus_unregister_object(dbus,
+			network_bss_get_path(network, entry->data));
 
 	l_dbus_unregister_object(dbus, network->object_path);
 
